<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Olomouc</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1479</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemian-hungarian-war-1468-1478">Bohemian–Hungarian War (1468–1478)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olomouc">Olomouc</a> of 1479 ended the war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladislaus-ii-of-bohemia">Vladislaus II of Bohemia</a> over the Bohemian crown. Both kept the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a>: Vladislaus held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> proper, while Matthias kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, Silesia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusatia">Lusatia</a>, which could be redeemed after his death. The lands returned to Vladislaus when he succeeded Matthias in Hungary in 1490.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-olomouc.jpg" alt="Peace of Olomouc" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michal Maňas · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olomoucka_smlouva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
